<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Building</h1>
<p>Valhalla is built by its players. Every zone, monster, object and quest in 
the game is written in the zone files of DikuMUD3, which are open source: 
anyone can read them, change them, and send in a new zone or a fix.
</p><p>To start building:
</p>
<ul><li>The source of the whole game, zones included, is on GitHub: <a rel="nofollow" class="external free" href="https://github.com/Seifert69/DikuMUD3">https://github.com/Seifert69/DikuMUD3</a></li>
<li>The DikuMUD wiki explains the zone language and DIL, the scripting language of the zones: <a rel="nofollow" class="external free" href="https://wiki.dikumud.com/wiki/DikuMUD">https://wiki.dikumud.com/wiki/DikuMUD</a> (start with "Getting started - Step by Step").</li>
<li>Talk with other builders on the builder channel (<a cmd='#'>comm add builder</a>; it is relayed to the game's Discord server).</li></ul>
<p>Valhalla likes unique zones: please don't send in a zone that is already on 
another mud. For a list of the builders who made the world, see 
<a cmd='#'>Help Creators</a>. The agreement builders signed in the old days is kept in 
<a cmd='#'>Help Builder Agreement</a>.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Creators</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Builder Agreement</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Comm</a>
</pre>




</div>